      "content": "That's a pretty bold stance. If the cash flow is so robust that the fine is already \"priced in,\" then why is the Solarix credit default swap (CDS) spread widening so rapidly right now? That usually indicates the market is pricing in a real possibility of a liquidity crunch, not just \"short-term noise.\" Can your system explain why the credit markets are signaling such high distress if your fundamentals model is seeing everything as stable?",
